  [A0] arbiter drift            : 6.20e-08
  [A1] ADP sum vs Ewald         : 3.76e-11

  PASS: the ADP's same-depth OPERATOR is correct. Its closed form,
  summed over the lattice, is exactly what the Ewald route resums --
  two independent constructions of the same object, agreeing at three
  Bloch vectors including two away from k_par = 0 where a phase-sign
  slip would show.

  So what the ADP needs for an unbounded medium is a RESUMMATION, not
  a reformulation. The composition is already verified at 5.1e-16
  (gate_rung5c) and the inter-plane half is already exact by
  reciprocal summation of the ADP's own vertical kernel. [A2] shows
  the size of what truncation costs at the table widths actually used.
